    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "contrast",
      "title": "Same Person or Another Person",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The key question is simple: does the object point back to the subject, or to a different person? If it points back, use the reflexive form. If it points to someone else, use an ordinary object pronoun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "For third person subjects, use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "seg",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " for the same person or group, but "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ham",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "henne",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "dem",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " for another person or group."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hun ser seg i speilet."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "She sees herself in the mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hun ser henne på bussen."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "She sees her on the bus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Han vasker seg."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "He washes himself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Han vasker ham."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "He washes him."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "With plural you, the reflexive form is "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "dere",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". With they, the reflexive form is "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "seg",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". This is a common place to check the subject carefully."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Dere hører dere selv på opptaket."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "You hear yourselves on the recording."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "De hører seg selv på opptaket."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "They hear themselves on the recording."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Where It Goes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "In a simple sentence, the reflexive pronoun usually comes after the finite verb. A finite verb is the verb that shows tense, such as "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "vasker",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ser",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Basic pattern: subject plus finite verb plus reflexive pronoun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Vi ser oss i speilet."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "We see ourselves in the mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg vasker meg om morgenen."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I wash myself in the morning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "note",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Some verbs often need a reflexive pronoun, and some verbs change meaning with one. For now, focus on the pronoun choice: same object as the subject means reflexive."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
